        'One of the vital scientific contributions of PEC’s deliberations—reflecting Prof. Shakil A. Romshoo’s dual engagement with atmospheric observation and Himalayan glaciology—has been insisting that Kashmir’s air pollution does not end at the hospital spirometer. Unlike sulfate aerosols that scatter incoming sunlight, black carbon (soot) and light-absorbing organic brown carbon generated by incomplete burning of damp orchard wood, domestic firewood, brick-kiln coal, and older diesel engines are potent short-lived climate forcers.',
