        'Every November, social media and urban talk shows discover rural smoke anew, condemning apple growers in Shopian, Kulgam, Pulwama, and Baramulla or urban custodians beneath Srinagar’s Chinars for setting leaf and twig piles ablaze. District Magistrates dutifully issue prohibitory orders under Section 144 CrPC (now Section 163 BNSS), threatening fines against open agricultural burning. Yet within forty-eight hours of every circular, thousands of small fires reappear across orchard terraces at dusk. Why?',
